WEBVTT

00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:15,880
Is it bad to eat butter if I'm supposed to be cancer-free?

00:00:15,880 --> 00:00:19,880
Oh, cancer-free? I think that person meant dairy-free.

00:00:19,880 --> 00:00:28,880
So if you're supposed to be dairy-free, and you are... can you eat butter?

00:00:28,880 --> 00:00:34,880
I get this question a lot. The problem is that yes, butter is dairy,

00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:41,880
and if dairy can be driving your cancer, then eating butter could be driving your cancer.

00:00:41,880 --> 00:00:45,880
However, the butter of substitutes that are out there,

00:00:45,880 --> 00:00:48,880
you know, can be worse for you.

00:00:48,880 --> 00:00:53,880
So I would say that, you know, if a person supposed to be dairy-free,

00:00:53,880 --> 00:00:55,880
can they eat a little bit of butter? Yes.

00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:58,880
I would say you'd better off eating a little bit of butter

00:00:58,880 --> 00:01:03,880
than eating the butter substitutes, margarine things that are out there.

00:01:03,880 --> 00:01:10,880
The plant oil-based butters, quote-a-quote, that are out there are not good for you.

00:01:10,880 --> 00:01:15,880
So, you know, there's other substitutes you can have coconut oil,

00:01:15,880 --> 00:01:20,880
you could have avocado oil and olive oil, but sometimes you need...

00:01:20,880 --> 00:01:26,880
you're putting butter on something is going to be more appropriate

00:01:26,880 --> 00:01:28,880
than using those other things.

00:01:28,880 --> 00:01:31,880
So, using a little bit of butter I would say is fine,

00:01:31,880 --> 00:01:34,880
even if you're supposed to be dairy-free.

00:01:34,880 --> 00:01:38,880
Remember, it's not a... it's a diet, it's not a religion.

00:01:38,880 --> 00:01:42,880
We're not forming a cult about your eating here.

00:01:42,880 --> 00:01:45,880
It's about taking a balanced approach,

00:01:45,880 --> 00:01:50,880
and okay, if dairy's driving my cancer, I'm going to stay 95% dairy-free.

00:01:50,880 --> 00:01:53,880
It doesn't mean you can't have some dairy.

00:01:53,880 --> 00:01:57,880
You know, a food sensitivity here, that if you eat that thing,

00:01:57,880 --> 00:01:59,880
you're going to cause inflammation.

00:01:59,880 --> 00:02:02,880
Let's say if you have gluten, you know, your antibodies,

00:02:02,880 --> 00:02:05,880
like the other question we had, they have glutinate antibodies,

00:02:05,880 --> 00:02:09,880
and you eat... well, I'm just going to... I'm pretty much gluten-free.

00:02:09,880 --> 00:02:12,880
Well, pretty much gluten-free is like being kind of pregnant.

00:02:12,880 --> 00:02:17,880
You're still going to cause inflammation every time you eat gluten,

00:02:17,880 --> 00:02:21,880
you know, three times a week, and if you have antibodies to,

00:02:21,880 --> 00:02:25,880
you know, brain cells, neural antibodies,

00:02:25,880 --> 00:02:29,880
you're going to cause inflammation of the brain in further destruction,

00:02:29,880 --> 00:02:33,880
so you can't just kind of go halfway at a diet like that.

00:02:33,880 --> 00:02:35,880
But when you're talking about what could be feeding cancer,

00:02:35,880 --> 00:02:39,880
if you've removed most of those things that you're...

00:02:39,880 --> 00:02:42,880
that you're consuming in what could be feeding cancer,

00:02:42,880 --> 00:02:46,880
then you've... you know, having a little bit of it

00:02:46,880 --> 00:02:49,880
isn't going to cause the cancer to take off and grow.

00:02:49,880 --> 00:02:52,880
So, it's about having that balance.

